Sam — adding a few practical snippets we use in onboarding (I left them short so your engs can paste into tests).

Node (basic client & retry helper):
```
import { RedwoodClient, RetryPolicy } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const retry = new RetryPolicy({ baseMs: 200, factor: 2, maxRetries: 4, retryOn: [502, 503, 'network'] });
await client.setRetryPolicy(retry);
const res = await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-alpha', prompt: 'Hello' });
```

Go (concurrency cap example):
```
// use a buffered channel as a semaphore to limit in-flight requests
sem := make(chan struct{}, 8) // cap concurrency at 8
for _, job := range jobs {
  sem <- struct{}{}
  go func(j Job) {
    defer func(){ <-sem }()
    // call Redwood endpoint
  }(job)
}
```

Timeout rules: set an overall request timeout (e.g. 30s) and smaller per-chunk timeouts for streaming. For retryable errors prefer full-jitter backoff.

I'll stand up a dev endpoint with a 100 qps burst window (subject to your acceptance test). Proposed tech sync: Thu 2026-05-06 10:00 PT. Is that good?

